    "title": "React Native Developer",
    "ciphertext": "~022078846821260105422",
    "description": "Key ResponsibilitiesFeature Delivery: \nArchitect, build, and deploy highly performant, cross-platform features across iOS and Android from a single codebase.\n\nUI/UX Implementation: Translate complex Figma designs into pixel-perfect, fluid, and responsive native-feeling interfaces.\n\nAPI Integration: Connect mobile frontends with secure backend services via REST APIs or GraphQL endpoints, handling async data states, local caching, and offline-first workflows.Performance \n\nTuning: Profile, diagnose, and resolve application bottlenecks, slow UI render passes, memory leaks, and JavaScript thread delays.\n\nNative Bridging: Write or integrate custom native modules and handle platform-specific APIs when React Native components fall short.\n\nQuality Assurance: Write clean, modular, and well-documented code backed by robust automated unit and integration tests.\n\nRequired Qualifications & SkillsExperience: \nMinimum 5 years of professional mobile development experience, with at least 4 years focused entirely on React Native.\n\nCore Languages: Deep proficiency in JavaScript, ES6+, and strong static typing skills using TypeScript.\n\nState Management: Mastery of modern state management libraries such as Redux, Zustand, or Context API.\n\nMobile Ecosystems: Solid working knowledge of iOS and Android platform fundamentals, layout engine constraints, and native build tools like Xcode and Android Studio.\n\nTesting: Proficiency using JavaScript testing frameworks such as Jest and React Native Testing Library.\n\nVersion Control: Expertise with Git workflows, including branching strategies and pull request reviews.",
